WEBVTT

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.350
I know it’s late.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:44.850
Is this the residence of Chouji-san,

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:48.550
the hairdresser who used to have access to the Saegusa mansion?

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:49.800
Yes.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.570
I was an employee of that mansion.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.830
Yaichi-san took care of me.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.740
I’m looking for the whereabouts of Yaichi-san.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.860
If you know anything...

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.980
I’m sorry to say that Yaichi-san has passed away.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:13.370
His son, the heir, also passed away soon after from an epidemic.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:15.550
Yaichi fell into a well.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.030
The grave?

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.570
Well... I’m not sure about that...

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.160
Sei, what did you do?

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.180
Your eyes are red.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.910
We haven’t been to Edo for a while.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.710
Let’s rest at the Hinagawa Inn.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.520
Hinagawa

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.430
I’m Take.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.420
What is your name?

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:03.820
Yaichi.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:12.810
How long are you planning to sleep there, Ichi?

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.930
This sure takes me way back to when we first met.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:27.610
You’d be all silent and brooding like you are now, looking for trouble... it was regrettable.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:33.110
But you weren’t that dirty, for a stray cat.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.440
The Dirty Stray Cat

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.850
Madam, give me that pipe.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.700
Is Sachi a burden?

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.500
Nope.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.490
She’s still a strange girl. She says she wants to be like me.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.120
I even told her I used to work in a brothel.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.540
Otake-dono?

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:14.210
Mm-hmm. Shinagawa’s. I used to live there.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.400
But that’s ancient history.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:23.040
But compared to the other girls, I was happy.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.620
Because he bought my freedom, I had to return to this fast life.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.610
You mean Yaichi-dono?

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:35.070
Perceptive as always, Masa.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.980
So do you know, Otake-dono?

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:43.170
About what? The crew Ichi-san was with in the past?

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:44.560
Yes.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.340
I don’t know, but you do, Masa.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.910
Uh, well...

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.790
You don’t have to tell me.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:57.830
If you want to be with Ichi-san for a long time, you shouldn’t let it concern you.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:02.830
He can easily tell if you do want to make it your business.

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:16.240
Brother, you’re accompanying me today, are you not?

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.240
Let us take a stroll around Edo.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.220
Here.

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:35.560
This is a large mansion.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.260
Akitsu!

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.050
Yagi-dono!

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.870
I am his sister, Sachi.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:50.140
She came here from my birth town.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.540
We have some delicious confections in the estate.

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:55.770
Akitsu, come with me.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:01.740
You’re too easy to read.

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:06.220
I can tell you’re trying to avoid me.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:25.360
Here.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.600
You’re as strong as I thought, Yagi-dono.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:31.810
Brother...

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:35.270
...your swordsmanship was supposed to be your lone strength.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:39.380
Come in, Akitsu. I’ll have some tea made.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:48.300
Did you lose on purpose?

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.870
No. That man is strong.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.040
Don’t show my swordsmanship?

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.660
Just act like you’re weak.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:02.660
Why?

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:07.550
He already knows that we, more or less, hang out with each other.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:12.020
You must act like the man he assumes you are.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:15.520
We can’t have him suspect us even more.

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.430
If he catches us, it’s all over.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:28.100
Is it all right if you don’t return to your office?

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:32.660
Well... If anything happens, someone will come running with the news.

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:42.770
There are maple trees larger than this one lining the streets next door to the Sawai Estate.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:47.250
At that time, it was a mansion belonging to a vassal named Saegusa.

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:50.780
You visited his grave back then, right?

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:55.480
His son was the one who died from the illness.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:02.170
My memories of the House of Sawai began right after my father chastised me.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.840
That happened to you, Yagi-dono? That’s hard to believe.

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:11.280
I was pretty debauched back then.

00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:16.210
When I returned that night, the gates were already closed.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:24.710
My father shouted to me from inside. “Foolish son, stay outside and cool your head!”

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.680
It was raining pretty hard at the time,

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:34.660
but I was still locked out and forced to get as soaked as a drowned rat.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:39.230
A servant for the House of Saegusa called out my name.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.560
Heizaemon-sama, this way.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.670
My neighbor...

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.200
You’ll catch a cold out here.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.030
Rice balls?

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:11.240
You might well become disinherited.

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:13.060
I’m fine with that.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.060
You are a strange man.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.210
He was named Yaichi.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:23.690
After that, we would see each other frequently, and he became my kindred spirit.

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:25.540
We were also around the same age.

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:28.940
The son they had there was excruciatingly serious.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:31.540
I teased him a lot.

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:34.160
I believe his name was Seinoshin...

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:36.860
He was a good kid.

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:42.430
I was really hurt when both of them died.

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.880
Seinoshin-sama!

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.510
What are you doing with him?

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:00.810
This is not the time for kids to be awake, Sei.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:02.310
I couldn’t sleep.

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.740
You’re drinking?

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:06.440
Yeah. Want some?

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:07.930
Hey, Heiza!

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:08.910
Huh?

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:10.110
...sama.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.520
Quit calling me “sama.”

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:15.570
Sei, sit here.

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:31.550
You two are very close.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:35.830
He’s a good friend.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:39.540
You must have friends, right? Like at the dojo.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:41.980
I do not.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:43.520
Hmm?

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:46.210
Yaichi is the only one I have.

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:54.200
You are a sorry fella.

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:58.490
In that case, I, Heiza, will be your friend.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:10:59.490
Huh?

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:02.500
What do you think? Now you have two.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:16.640
Mother!

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:19.320
What is it?

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.160
It’s Ichi-san.

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:24.890
Don’t you think he’s been acting weird for the past few days?

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:29.520
He has really been absent-minded.
He doesn’t hear us when we call him.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:33.090
Is there something wrong with him?

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:34.760
He’s probably lovesick.

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:35.870
Go back.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:45.610
It hasn’t been the past few days. It’s been since that ronin arrived.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:53.190
I need to ask you one thing.

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:54.890
What is it?

00:11:55.950 --> 00:12:02.770
This man you’re close with, Yaichi-dono: is there a burn scar on his left shoulder?

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:07.520
I haven’t had a chance to see.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:10.970
Is that so? Very well then.

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:15.990
Still, that guy does bear a resemblance.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:36.340
Cat... cat?

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.080
I’m returning home.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:03.420
Really?

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:09.480
When I saw Otake-san, I started to long for Chuujirou-sama.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:15.170
However, I need you to write a few words for me.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:20.280
Write “I am opposed to the arranged marriage.” to Brother Bun.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:26.520
I don’t think my words will have any effect.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:30.400
You must be more reliable, Brother!

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:40.880
Even if Brother Bun is the head of the household,

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:46.460
as long as you’re around, your little brother and sister will not disobey you!

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:50.980
But did you not stay when I told you to go home...?

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:54.880
It was not the right time or circumstances!

00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:00.340
Matsukichi-san!

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:07.770
I want to thank you for the hairpin.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:09.600
Sure.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.650
Good. It’s becoming.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:18.530
Um, I have suitors back home.

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:19.600
Oh.

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:23.950
I’m sorry, but can I still have this hairpin?

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:25.640
Sure.

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:29.030
It will be my memory of Edo...

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:33.220
Are you leaving? Stay safe.

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:36.030
Ah... uh-huh.

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:47.780
Brother, that was painful.

00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:52.140
I am a woman of sin.

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:54.100
Hmm?

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:03.160
You don’t hear a lot about Edo living out here.

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:08.120
You coming here with news really helps me out, Toku-san.

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:12.580
I spoke with a man at Hiratsuka.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:16.450
It was about the last of the Kuhei crew of Bakuro.

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:20.570
A man with a large scar on his left side.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:28.070
He said something about looking for his old comrade and asked if I had any information.

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:30.050
An old comrade?

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:37.930
That’s the first time I’ve heard of that man. Someone named Seinoshin.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:39.650
You know him?

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:43.190
Why is that man looking around?

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:51.770
He said when the Bakuro crew was apprehended, there was talk that this Seinoshin was the traitor.

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:56.840
Do you know, Souji-don’?

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:59.590
I saw the man himself

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.300
just the other day.

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:08.930
Toku-san, can you keep the stuff about that guy to yourself?

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:14.810
Of course I can. Tell me what to do, and it’s done.

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:19.960
I need to tell Ume-dono about this.

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:24.250
Katsuraya

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:29.960
Now, tell us about your woman, Sensei.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.410
Can you please refrain from that?

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:35.450
Then choose one of us.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.660
One whose looks best suit your tastes.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:39.880
It’s just...

00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:43.150
All right, tell us about your town, Sensei.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:48.220
We’re asking for an enjoyable story.

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:50.150
You’re so stupid.

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:54.440
If you ask him for an enjoyable story, he’ll start to yearn for his town.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:07.160
I will... go buy some confections.

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:09.130
Oh, that’s great!

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:15.040
He’s become quite an attentive man.

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:18.020
Sensei was that way from the start.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.960
He’s very sweet.

00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:28.050
Please don’t do anything unnecessary.

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:36.520
When those women remember their birthplaces, they seem so sad.

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:41.580
I was thinking that if their lifestyles were not always so trying,

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:46.950
they wouldn’t think about their hometowns and feel so anguished.

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:50.240
You’re a forward-looking man, much to my surprise.

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:55.420
I probably got that from Yaichi-dono.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:58.370
“Enjoy each day as they come.”

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:01.230
I thought “That makes sense.” when I heard it.

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:04.580
It’s all thanks to Yaichi-dono.

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:17.110
Don’t tell them what you can’t do for yourself, Ichi.

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:34.220
Get rid of anyone who gets in your way.

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:36.810
Anyone.

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:17.750
Yagi-dono!

00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:23.650
You’re sure burning the midnight oil.

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:25.710
Yagi-dono.

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:28.210
What is it?

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:32.180
There was something yesterday that piqued my interest.

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:33.640
Hmm?

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:37.600
There wasn’t a burn scar on Yaichi-dono’s shoulder.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:41.560
I don’t remember asking you to check.

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:46.520
I thought it would be right to tell you.

00:19:48.010 --> 00:19:48.940
Okay.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:55.840
Next time, we’ll have some soba.

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:08.900
Akitsu is such a terrible liar.

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:16.870
So, he really is Seinoshin, huh?

00:20:23.270 --> 00:20:26.230
Seinoshin-sama, take a look.

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:29.740
It’s so beautiful and magnificent.

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:32.710
Believe in yourself.

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:39.950
The scar from that burning is the same shape as a maple leaf, right?

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.940
To be

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.940
continued

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:16.140
I’ve got a feeling that something was hidden

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:25.430
in the words you once told me. Those words cross my mind again and again.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:33.850
Yet your voice always sounds the same as before.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:33.850
Kimi no koe ga ima no kawarazuni kikoeteirunda

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:40.900
Every time I breathe, I wanna hold you in my arms

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:49.830
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:57.910
Every time I breathe, I just wanna hold you in my arms again

00:21:59.030 --> 00:22:06.730
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:07.390 --> 00:22:14.970
Every day I need you  All the time I'll be there for you

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:24.080
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:33.200
Next time on House of Five Leaves:

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:34.710
This is Jin.

00:22:35.270 --> 00:22:37.400
I have a large scar on my left side.

00:22:38.090 --> 00:22:39.260
You’re wondering, right?

00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:46.520
Too bad there’s no time to tell you about the horrible events that led up to that wound.

00:22:46.520 --> 00:22:48.010
Well then, the next episode’s title is:

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:49.930
“Pardon My Rudeness.”
